  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.48–0.65) vastly outperform image-only (0.21), and the best RNA config is scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (0.650). The critical open question is whether adding the image modality via fusion can complement the strong RNA signal or will dilute it. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests that question with the simplest fusion (concat) and the same image encoder (resnet50) already characterized in isolation. If it beats 0.650, multimodal fusion is a promising direction and we can then explore better image encoders (ViT-L) and weighted fusion. If it underperforms, we learn that the weak image features (0.208 standalone) do not contribute useful complementary signal, saving budget from exploring the many multimodal variants. This single experiment resolves the highest-uncertainty design decision (modality combination) before committing budget to finer-grained fusion/encoder variations."
}

